import sys
p = sys.argv[1]
lines = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\n')
idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith('| 657 |')]
assert len(idx) == 1
lines.insert(idx[0] + 1, "| 658 | 2026-10-25 | **Chapter 5, Hand Positions: the Beginner floor's new technique room (her answer: option 1 for room 5; asked 'five-finger positions, then a one-octave scale?' -> yes: chapter 1's thumb in and out, chapter 5's C and G positions, Tones & semitones' five-finger positions in every key, then Scales' one octave with thumb under and 3 over on the Prelim - Grade 1 floor).** Built on row 657. Its Lesson Book is its online lesson (hpLbPages, 8 pages, the chapter 1 frame): opener ('Five fingers, five keys, one finger on each: that is a hand position.'); Step 1 C position (middle C 'the C just left of the small house in the middle', right thumb 1 on middle C, left 5 on the C below; 'One finger, one key.'); Step 2 G position (the same shape, G 'the second white key of a big house'; puzzle: which finger plays C?); Step 3 Move between them ('the arm carries the hand': lift, travel, land; one silent beat to move); Step 4 Hands together (the same numbers together, 'mirror twins', contrary motion); Step 5 Taking turns (Echo: the left hand answers with the same letters, lower); Play: four tunes by finger numbers, our own (Up and down the street, The left hand climbs too, Over to G, Mirror twins), one circle a steady beat; My five checks. On the keys only: no staff before chapter 7 (The staff); Steps & skips keeps its C and G position pages, on the staff. Live: HpPosPad, HpMovePad, HpTogetherPad, HpRows (listen); print: a pen keyboard with finger circles (hpKeysRaw on sskKeysRaw). Drill, five levels: which finger (C), find the key (C, tap), which finger (G), which hand and which position (letters hidden), mirror twins (the other hand's same finger; right keys over left). House icon: five keys and five fingertips. The Home's Positions concept now asks this chapter's questions (was Posture level 3). ROOM_AFTER follows the new order (Steps & skips after The staff and Hand positions; Dynamics after Steps & skips and Time signatures, for the tie); chapter lists tag each chapter with its floor (the old grade tags predate the floors). **Not yet:** its Workbook and teacher's copy; Listen and sing (room 6). Files: drills.html, drills.src.html, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/patch682.py, _workspace/concept-book-kit/sc/hp682.jsx. |")
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write('\n'.join(lines)); print('ok')
